{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1384485-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-6-grave-encounter","id":1384485,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 6 - Grave Encounter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-28T13:05:39-07:00","id":1384485,"title":"Unchained in Manch-Vegas: Session 6 - Grave Encounter","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cast:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Liberty Griswald</b> - Guardian/Tempter. Works as a Bodyguard for the Empire Security Company.</li> <li><b>Molly Underwood - </b>Destroyer/Tempter. Works as a Private Investigator and part time movie theater attendant.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Mini-Session 5.5 Summary:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In an earlier unposted session Liberty brushed off Detective Jane Bullet. She pressed him on the similarities of his killing of some would be kidnappers and a shooting at a Dunkin Donuts. He took her card, but decided to call it a night.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Session 6 Summary:</span></span> </b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While Liberty purchases a Knock-Out Punch driving glove gadget, Molly was busy investigating their new boss Ms. White. Molly met up with Zacharia at the Library. He told Molly that Ms. White was a typical Saboteur as far as he knew. He\u2019d trust her with God-Machine related news, but cautions to keep her at arm\u2019s length in regards to any information about their Covers or personal life.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Zacharia promised Molly he would try and help her when he can. He gave her a missing person\u2019s case that he had come across. Molly expertly solved the case and asked for monetary payment (Exceptional Success, I gave her the Inspired Condition). Molly decided to accept </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">During the night Molly and Liberty hear thunder. Liberty realizes that this is probably the Seamstress making his Knock-out Punch Driving Glove gadget. Not knowing what the thunder is, Molly checks on the God-Machine agents they are tracking. They appear to be investigating a nearby cemetery.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Molly and Liberty meetup at the cemetery and discover that the Seamstress is trying to evade capture. Sadly Liberty did more harm than good and gave away his and her position. One of the agents shot at them. Circling around the agent, Molly was able to plug into him and remove his memory of the last hour (Memory Theft) and replace it with accidentally shooting a deer. She discovered that the agents were being organized by the same Angel who was organizing the Sleeper Agent drug ring within the city. She doesn't hear the words Demon or Angel being used, but does know these are agents of the God-Machine.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The three demons make their escape while the Agents believe they shot a deer. The Seamstress slaps Liberty and admonishes him for almost exposing her Cover. She then gives Molly a Janitor\u2019s Uniform gadget with the Authorized embed stitched into it. Molly was grateful, but also saw that the Seamstress had animal entrails sitting around in her shop.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">GM Notes:</span></span></b><ul><li><b>Preparation</b>.<ul><li>Work I did before hand:<ul><li>Updated my Roll20 character sheets to the official Chronicles of Darkness sheet.</li> <li>Created macros for everyone of my players. (Sadly I can't figure out how to make them smart enough to update on their own)</li> <li>Created stat lines for the Men In Black Stigmatics as antagonists.</li> <li>Updated my quick reference material</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Session Start</b><ul><li>Two of my players showed up, but we have realized that we can't have game this coming weekend because of</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What could I have done better:</b><ul><li>I'm still uncomfortable with Conditions.</li> <li>I need better quick reference material for myself. I have a DM Screen, but it's missing some key information for me.</li> <li>I am making an XP tracker because it's getting hard to tell people what they can do with it.</li> <li>I am unfamiliar with the combat, so I rolled 5 successes on my NPC's shot at a PC resulting in 5 Lethal damage I believe? I subtracted 2 successes because the player was in cover behind a gravestone, but it felt pretty wrong to me.</li> <li>Liberty's player let me know he would have told Molly that the lightning strike was just his gloves being made and that he wouldn't have gone investigating with her if he had known. Because he didn't think the Seamstress would have been at risk of getting caught by the Men In Black. I should give him more prompts in the future. I should have said you realize that Molly is going in the same direction of the lightning strike that you know was the Seamstress's doing.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>What went well:</b><ul><li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">My quick reference material worked.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Everyone liked the macros a lot better than what we previously had to do.</span></li> </ul></li> <li><b>What do I need to not forget:</b><ul><li>Liberty Griswald<ul><li>He fired a shot in the graveyard, which means even with the memory manipulation one of the Men in Black knows that there were more gunshots fired than what their partner shot.</li> <li>Liberty was injured so there is likely blood at the scene.</li> </ul></li> <li>Jane Bullet (NPC)<ul><li>Jane's card may or may not be a Gadget to detect Aether, at this point I'm saying no because I feel like Demons can sense Gadgets quite easily.</li> </ul></li> <li>Molly Underwood<ul><li>Ms. White is someone Molly doesn't trust so I may focus on that next session.</li> </ul></li> <li>Seamstress<ul><li>\u200bShe respects Molly.</li> <li>She is starting to think that Liberty is incompetent, because he gave away their hiding spot.</li> </ul></li> <li>Men In Black<ul><li>\u200bThey may suspect something is amiss, which could cause them to discover the tracking device on their car and set a trap for the players.</li> <li>They need some Supernatural Merits to make them different than average NPCs.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li><b>Notes for Next Session:</b><ul><li>If Alan is able to make it to next session he may need gear.</li> <li>The raid on the Men in Black base will likely be next session.</li> </ul></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Please let me know what you think.<br /> <br /> Additionally I have the following questions:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do I calculate damage? And how is it healed? Looking at the book it seems like it takes about two days to heal 1 damage a day. And it seems that Aggravated damage (Which I haven't used yet) isn't mentioned.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What might the Men In Black base look like? These are two Stigmatics who are taking orders from an Angel, but I suspect that their office is a small unremarkable office space in an office building, hidden among dentists and lawyer offices.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":". 04-28-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T15:23:25-07:00","id":1384727,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DontEatRawHagis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1384485-unchained-in-manch-vegas-session-6-grave-encounter#post1384485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> Additionally I have the following questions:</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">How do I calculate damage? And how is it healed? Looking at the book it seems like it takes about two days to heal 1 damage a day. And it seems that Aggravated damage (Which I haven't used yet) isn't mentioned.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What might the Men In Black base look like? These are two Stigmatics who are taking orders from an Angel, but I suspect that their office is a small unremarkable office space in an office building, hidden among dentists and lawyer offices.</span></span></li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>From the CoD core book:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wounds recover at the following rates:<ul><li>Bashing: One point per 15 minutes.</li> <li>Lethal: One point per two days.</li> <li>Aggravated: One point per week.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><br /> I assume that the MiB look like standard MiB, and you are looking for that extra bit of strangeness that throws things off. The MiB might have a small Glitch. </span><ul><li>Metallic eyes (hidden by their ever-present sunglasses).</li> <li>Tattoo on the back of their neck.</li> <li>No actual mouth - just lips.</li> <li>Phones, TVs and radios just put out static when they are near.</li> </ul>Is that the sort of thing you are looking for?<br /> <br /> <br /> </span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24502-kieranmullen","name":"KieranMullen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}